   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The functions \\( f \\) and \\( g \\) are differentiable, with \\( f(3) = 2 \\) and \\( f'(3) = -3 \\). The line tangent to the graph of \\( g \\) at \\( x = 3 \\) has equation \\( y = 2 x - 2 \\). Let \\( h(x) = f(x)g(x) \\). Find the value of \\( h'(3) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": -8
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Record the values at \\( x = 3 \\): \\( f(3) = 2 \\), \\( f'(3) = -3 \\). The tangent line gives \\( g(3) = 4 \\) (its height at \\( x = 3 \\)) and \\( g'(3) = 2 \\) (its slope).",
         "mathjson": -3
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule, \\( (fg)'(3) = f'(3)g(3) + f(3)g'(3) \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Substitute: \\( (-3)(4) + (2)(2) = -8 \\).",
         "mathjson": -8
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( h'(3) = -8 \\).",
         "mathjson": -8
      }
   ],
